Firstly, we filter out any non-binary operator expressions and appended them to result list. Here the if condition is checking if the expression is binary or not. In a binary expression the expression can take 2 operators.

Secondly, if the expression has an operator of "&" then we evaluate the result as,
* If the left side of the operator is the same as the right side we return the left side.
* If the left side is the complement of the right side we return the left side and the right side.
* In all other cases, we raise a `ValueError` exception.

Thirdly, if the expression has an operator of "|" then we evaluate the result as,
* If the left side of the operator is the same as the right side we return the left side.
* If the left side is the complement of the right side we return the left side.
* If the left side is not the complement of the right side we return the left side and the right side.

Lastly, we raise a `ValueError` if the expression does not satisfy any one of the above conditions.

